        <briefdescription>
<para>This function validates the parameters of the ML-DSA signature generation which takes its rnd from the request, an algorithm validation only service. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>MldsaParamsPtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the <ref refid="struct_x_asu___mldsa_sign_derand_params" kindref="compound">XAsu_MldsaSignDerandParams</ref> structure which holds the ML-DSA signature generation parameters and the rnd to sign with.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>XST_SUCCESS, if validation of ML-DSA parameters is successful.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XST_FAILURE, if any argument is invalid. </para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
<para>Validate ML-DSA params pointer.</para><para>Validate the signing parameters this command shares with signature generation.</para><para>The secret key comes from KeyAddr only, as the key vault is not reachable from a validation command.</para><para>rnd must be supplied: a zero address is an error here rather than a request to draw from the TRNG.</para>        </inbodydescription>
